WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.000
<v NARRATOR>In the early eighteen hundreds,
a lighthouse was a fire in a box. Most of

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.200
its light went up into the sky, or down
into the rocks.

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:12.050
<v NARRATOR>Ships could not see it until

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:15.970
they were already close. Too close, on a
stormy night.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:20.990
<v NARRATOR>In eighteen twenty-two, a French
engineer named Augustin Fresnel showed a

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:26.930
different lens. Not one thick slab of
glass, but rings of thin prisms, stepped

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:27.710
like a staircase.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:33.130
<v NARRATOR>Each ring bent the light the
same way. Together they threw almost all

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:34.010
of it toward the sea.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:38.560
<v KEEPER>The first night we lit it, the
beam reached the far headland. We just

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.120
stood there and watched it turn.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:45.230
<v NARRATOR>A year later, the lens was
shining from the Cordouan lighthouse.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:51.350
Within a few decades, lights like it
guarded coasts around the world.
